    "reviewed_findings": [
      "All 24 entries in the fixed formal scope match their declared SHA-256; all seven blessing pages and the config/draft/image/primary receipts are covered.",
      "The actual shared-map record is one melee blessing and one trait variant for ogryn_club_p1, bound to Mk I / Mk II / Mk III mark IDs; the reverse shovel page, weapon README, blessing catalog, melee catalog, glossary, and links point to the same entry and icon.",
      "The UI/RAW receipt supports Latrine Shovel Brute-Brainer Mk III, Mk XIX, and Mk V. The formal text distinguishes Mk III special uppercut from folded-mode special light/heavy hits on Mk XIX/V; folding alone does not hit, and a folded special hit unfolds the shovel so another folded trigger requires toggling again.",
      "Tier values are additive melee critical-chance inputs of +7.5 / +10 / +12.5 / +15 percentage points for 3 seconds. The own map replaces the generic fallback rather than adding to it. The held-slot gate also controls the ongoing stat; switching slots stops its contribution while the timer continues, and removal of the equipped blessing removes its instance.",
      "The action-start critical flag is fixed before its hit events. The new proc cannot retroactively change the triggering action; later actions can use it after the buff/stat cache update. An already active, unexpired window can benefit an action that starts before it expires.",
      "A qualifying hit restarts the 3-second window when its blessing proc event is processed, not at an assumed raw-hit timestamp; expiry is strict, refresh does not stack, and the updated README/config/draft/resume wording agrees.",
      "Normal attacks, charged attacks, and push-follow attacks do not trigger the blessing; qualifying melee special profiles do. Push-follow can use an active melee critical chance input; pure push is a push attack and has no melee crit roll.",
      "The two IV-tier examples correctly treat +15 percentage points as additive chance: 5% to 20% (a 300% relative increase over the assumed 5% input), and 15% to 30% when another 10-point input exists (a 100% relative increase); neither claims a final-damage increase. Clamp and chance-to-damage conversion order match the cited crit consumer.",
      "The localization page gives exact EN and zh-TW four-tier placeholder substitutions for chance and duration; the RAW wording is not presented as a contradiction. Icon path and attachment URL are distinct and agree with the image receipt."
    ],
